|-|Parameters=
=== Parameters ===

==== Grid-level parameters ====

{| class="wikitable"
! Parameter !! Description !! Required?
|-
| variant || Card style for the whole grid: <code>default</code>, <code>fullimage</code>, or <code>compact</code>. See the ''Variants'' tab. Unknown or empty values fall back to <code>default</code>. || No
|-
| perrow || Maximum number of cards per row. If omitted, the module picks a balanced split automatically (e.g. 6 members → 3/3, 5 → 3/2, 7 → 4/3) instead of letting rows wrap unevenly like 5/1. Narrow screens still wrap to fewer per row. || No
|-
| fit || How portraits fill their frame, for the whole grid. Default crops to fill (<code>cover</code>); set <code>contain</code> to show the whole image letterboxed — useful for tall full-body renders. || No
|-
| imgpos || Which part of the portrait to keep when cropping, for the whole grid. Any CSS <code>object-position</code> value, e.g. <code>top</code> (keeps faces in full-body art), <code>center</code>, <code>50% 20%</code>. || No
|}

==== Per-member parameters (replace # with 1, 2, 3, …) ====

{| class="wikitable"
! Parameter !! Description !! Required?
|-
| name# || The name of the utaite unit member. Also the link target for the name and portrait. || Yes
|-
| image# || The filename of the member's portrait image. This should be an image that has been uploaded to the wiki. (<code>img#</code> also works.) || No
|-
| desc# || Short description of the member, e.g. Dice no. 1 for Liura from Ireisu. || No
|-
| color# || The member's associated color. Hex (e.g. <code>#a9276d</code>) or a CSS color name (e.g. <code>Red</code>). Shown as a swatch + value, and used for the card's accent (top bar / name dot / left edge, depending on variant). Invalid values fall back to the wiki theme color. || No
|-
| fanname# || The member's fans name. || No
|-
| oshimark# || The member's oshi mark, typically an emoji, special character, or a small image like <code><nowiki>[[File:Sixfonia.png|16x16px]]</nowiki></code>. || No
|-
| status# || The member's current status (e.g., active, inactive, hiatus). Case-insensitive. Default is active. || No
|-
| leader# || '''Only add this parameter if he/she/they are a leader of the group.''' You can fill this parameter with "yes" without quotation mark. A crown badge appears on the card and expands to a "LEADER" label on hover. More than one member can be a leader. || No
|-
| fit# || Per-member override of the grid-level <code>fit</code> parameter (<code>contain</code> to letterbox this member's portrait only). || No
|-
| imgpos# || Per-member override of the grid-level <code>imgpos</code> parameter, e.g. <code>top</code> for one member whose full-body render gets cropped badly. || No
|}

==== Regarding Status Parameter ====
* '''active''': Currently an active member of the group and actively performing as an utaite.
* '''hiatus''': Temporarily paused from activities, but still a member of the group.
* '''inactive''': Not currently performing as an utaite.
* '''graduated''': Former member who has officially left the group.
* '''terminated''': The member's contract or association with the group was forcibly ended due to serious issues, such as a scandal. Terminated members are rendered as plain text — neither the name nor the portrait links to their page. You should still use the [[:Template:TerminatedUtaiteGroupMember|Terminated Utaite Group Member Template]] to exclude terminated members from the [[:Category:Utaite_Groups|Utaite Groups Category Page]]/[[Template:UtaiteGroupGallery|Utaite Group Gallery Template]].

Statuses outside this list are displayed as written but styled like <code>active</code>.

|-|Variants=
=== Variants ===

The <code>variant</code> parameter switches the card style for the whole grid.

==== default ====
Vertical 200px card: color bar on top, portrait, then one info line each for description, color, fan name, oshi mark, and a status pill.

{{UtaiteUnitMember
|image1=template_doc.png
|name1=Member Name
|desc1=Member Description
|color1=Red
|fanname1=yessir
|oshimark1=🎤
|status1=inactive
}}

==== fullimage ====
200×280 card where the portrait fills the whole card — best for transparent-background renders. The name sits on a bottom gradient overlay with a dot in the member's color; a rotated corner ribbon shows the status; extra info (description, fan name, oshi mark, color) slides up on hover. Graduated and terminated members are desaturated until hovered.

<pre>
{{UtaiteUnitMember
|variant=fullimage
|image1=... |name1=... (same per-member parameters)
}}
</pre>

{{UtaiteUnitMember
|variant=fullimage
|image1=template_doc.png
|name1=Member Name
|desc1=Member Description
|color1=Red
|fanname1=yessir
|oshimark1=🎤
|leader1=yes
}}

==== compact ====
Small horizontal 250px card: portrait strip on the left, a 4px edge in the member's color, name + description + status on the right. Fan name and color are revealed on hover. Good for large rosters or sidebar-ish sections.

<pre>
{{UtaiteUnitMember
|variant=compact
|image1=... |name1=... (same per-member parameters)
}}
</pre>

{{UtaiteUnitMember
|variant=compact
|image1=template_doc.png
|name1=Member Name
|desc1=Member Description
|color1=Red
|fanname1=yessir
|oshimark1=🎤
}}

|-|Styling=
=== Styling ===

Cards are laid out in a centered, wrapping flex grid with a 16px gap; they wrap to the next line as needed, depending on the page width and the number of members. All CSS classes are prefixed <code>uum-</code> and live in [[MediaWiki:Common.css]]. The design uses Citizen skin custom properties with fixed fallbacks, so it holds up in both light and dark mode.

==== Regarding the styling based on the utaite status ====
Each status has a fixed color used by the status pill (default), corner ribbon (fullimage), and status line (compact):
* active — green
* hiatus — orange
* inactive — grey
* graduated — purple (card dimmed in fullimage/compact)
* '''terminated''' — red (card dimmed in fullimage/compact; name and portrait unlinked)

