|-|Legacy syntax=
=== Legacy syntax (deprecated) ===

Before the module rewrite, each member was a separate transclusion using unnumbered parameters, wrapped in a manual flex <code>&lt;div&gt;</code>:

<pre>
<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; gap: 20px;text-align: center;">
{{UtaiteUnitMember
|image=Member1.jpg
|name=Member 1
|color=Red
|leader=yes
}}
{{UtaiteUnitMember
|image=Member2.jpg
|name=Member 2
|color=Blue
}}
</div>
</pre>

This '''still renders''' — the module falls back to unnumbered parameters when no <code>name1</code> is present, treating the transclusion as a single-member grid — but it is deprecated. Pages still using it are collected in [[:Category:Pages using legacy UtaiteUnitMember syntax]]; please migrate them to the numbered syntax and remove the wrapper <code>&lt;div&gt;</code>.

|-|Notes=
=== Notes ===

* Make sure to upload the member images to the wiki before using them in the template.
* Only <code>name#</code> is required per member. Optional fields that are not provided simply do not appear on the card (status always appears, defaulting to active).
* Number members consecutively — the module stops at the first missing <code>name#</code>.
* Rows wrap symmetrically: with more members than fit one row, the module caps the grid width so e.g. 6 members render as 3/3 rather than 5/1. Use <code>perrow</code> to force a specific maximum per row. Legacy (unnumbered) transclusions can't do this, since each one only knows about its own single member.
* Portraits are cropped to fill their frame by default (<code>object-fit: cover</code>, center crop). If members' art gets cropped badly — e.g. tall full-body renders losing heads — set <code>imgpos=top</code> to crop from the bottom instead, or <code>fit=contain</code> to letterbox the whole image. Both work grid-wide or per member (<code>imgpos3=top</code>).
* To change the overall layout or styling of the cards, edit the <code>uum-</code> rules in [[MediaWiki:Common.css]]; to change structure or parameters, edit [[Module:UtaiteUnitMember]]. The template page itself is only a thin <code>#invoke</code> wrapper.
